      "message": "WebKit Bugzilla\nAttachment #280982: Patch for bug #158601\nHome | New | Browse | Search |  \n  Search [?] | Reports | Requests | New Account | Log In | Forgot Password\nView | Details | Raw Unified | Return to bug 158601 | Differences between   and this patch  Diff \nCollapse All | Expand All \n\n(-)a/Source/WebCore/ChangeLog (+94 lines)\nLines 1-3 Link Here\n1\t2016-06-09  Benjamin Poulain  \u003cbpoulain@apple.com\u003e\n2\t\n3\t        Add support for passive event listeners on touch events\n4\t        https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id\u003d158601\n5\t\n6\t        Reviewed by NOBODY (OOPS!).\n7\t\n8\t        This patch wires \"passive\" state of EventTarget to the delivery of touch\n9\t        events in WebKit2.\n10\t\n11\t        Instead of having a NonFastScrollableRegion, we have a pair of regions\n12\t        in EventTrackingRegions.\n13\t        The \"asynchronousDispatchRegion\" tracks the area for which all event\n14\t        listeners are passive. For those, events should be dispatched asynchronously.\n15\t        The \"synchronousDispatchRegion\" tracks the area for which there is at\n16\t        least one active event listener. Events have to be dispatched synchronously\n17\t        for correctness.\n18\t\n19\t        Tests: fast/events/touch/ios/tap-with-active-listener-on-elements.html\n20\t               fast/events/touch/ios/tap-with-active-listener-on-window.html\n21\t               fast/events/touch/ios/tap-with-passive-listener-on-elements.html\n22\t               fast/events/touch/ios/tap-with-passive-listener-on-window.html\n23\t\n24\t        * WebCore.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj:\n25\t        * dom/Document.cpp:\n26\t        (WebCore::Document::wheelEventHandlersChanged):\n27\t        (WebCore::Document::Document): Deleted.\n28\t        * dom/Document.h:\n29\t\n30\t        * dom/EventListenerMap.cpp:\n31\t        (WebCore::EventListenerMap::containsActive):\n32\t        If a Target has multiple listener for an event type